# A loop keeps an unwritten slot precise while writing another slot

Verifies constant indexing keeps the flow state per element. The loop rewrites
`a[1]`, so only that slot loses its recorded subtype while `a[0]` still adds as
`10mm + 1mm = 11mm` and the rewritten slot reads back as `30cm`.

>>> source
let a = [10mm, 20cm]

for (i in 0..3) {
    a[1] = 30cm
    print(a[0] + 1mm)
}

print(a[1])

<<< stdout
11mm
11mm
11mm
30cm

<<< stderr
